Short:        Rocket.Chat client (ReAction, AmiSSL)
Author:       Tommy Frössman
Uploader:     Tommy Frössman
Type:         comm/net
Version:      0.1
Requires:     AmigaOS 3.2, 68020+, bsdsocket.library, AmiSSL 5.1+
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.2.0

AmiRocket is a native Rocket.Chat client for AmigaOS 3.2. It connects to
ordinary self-hosted Rocket.Chat servers over HTTPS.

Features
 - Login with user name and password, two-factor codes (authenticator app
   or e-mail), remembered login via auth token
 - Public channels, private groups and direct messages with unread counts
 - Message history, sending, and new/edited/deleted messages by polling
 - UTF-8 <-> ISO-8859-1 conversion with readable fallbacks for quotes,
   dashes and common emoji
 - Network code runs in its own process: the GUI never blocks
 - SELFTEST and PROBE Shell modes for checking the setup

Installation
 Copy AmiRocket anywhere and start it. AmiSSL 5 must be installed for
 https:// servers. Settings are stored in ENVARC:AmiRocket.prefs.

Shell usage
 AmiRocket SELFTEST
 AmiRocket PROBE=https://chat.example.com [USER=name PASSWORD=pw] [CODE=n]

Note: with "Remember login" enabled, the Rocket.Chat auth token is
stored in ENVARC:AmiRocket.prefs. Use Project/Log out to revoke it.
